desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Hooks Relative Script Path"
	title_zh: "检测到 Hook 使用相对脚本路径",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-config-hooks-relative-script-path"
	risk: "security-misconfiguration"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `hooks-relative-script-path-bash` (upstream/ai/ai-best-practices/hooks-relative-script-path/hooks-relative-script-path.yaml).
Original message: Relative path used for script invocation in hook. Use absolute paths or environment variables like $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, $CURSOR_PROJECT_DIR, or $HOME to ensure the correct script is executed regardless of working directory.

CWE: CWE-426: Untrusted Search Path
References:
- https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks
- https://cursor.com/docs/agent/hooks
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Use absolute paths or project-directory environment variables such as $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR or $CURSOR_PROJECT_DIR to invoke hook scripts.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.sh": <<<POS
source ./scripts/check.sh
POS
	"safefile://neg.sh": <<<NEG
source /opt/project/scripts/check.sh
NEG
)

${*.sh}.pattern_regex(/(?:source|bash|sh|\.)\s+\.\/\S+/) as $p0
${*.bash}.pattern_regex(/(?:source|bash|sh|\.)\s+\.\/\S+/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Hooks Relative Script Path",
	title_zh: "检测到 Hook 使用相对脚本路径",
	message: "Relative script path used in a hook; the working directory may be attacker-controlled.",
}
